# Output / result directories.
# BOTH cases, deliberately: the directory this repo actually writes is
# lowercase `results/`, and for a long time only `Results/` was listed. That
# matched anyway on macOS, whose filesystem is case-insensitive, and matched
# NOTHING on Linux — so `results/` and `tools/results/` were untracked noise on
# every case-sensitive checkout, including CI, while looking perfectly ignored
# to whoever wrote the rule. No leading slash, so both match at any depth.
results/
Results/

# Mesh exports. Every mesh run writes these, and it writes them next to whatever
# geometry or config it was launched from — not just under results/ — so they
# turn up in examples/geometries/, config/mesh/ and the repo root. Matched by
# extension because none of the four has ever been tracked (`git ls-files`), and
# a reference grid worth keeping can still go in with `git add -f`.
*.vtk
*.vrt
*.cel
*.bnd

# Solver pipeline binaries + case data (large prebuilt binaries, kept out of VCS)
solver/

# Editor / tooling artifacts
.antigravitycli/
# Browser "save page as" sidecar folders (docs/**/ *.html.download/)
*.html.download/

# Claude Code runtime state. NOT the same thing as `.agents/` + `skills-lock.json`,
# which ARE tracked: those pin which skills this repo uses, the way a lockfile
# does, and `docs/agents/` is referenced by CLAUDE.md. This directory otherwise
# holds per-machine runtime state (scheduled_tasks.lock, skills/).
#
# Two entries are exceptions and must be tracked. `settings.json` carries the
# SessionStart hook that measures the architecture backlog, which is a property
# of THIS REPO rather than of one developer's machine — an ignored copy would
# fire for whoever happened to create it and for nobody else. `rules/` holds the
# path-scoped instruction files (#59/#62): they govern the repo, are named by
# CLAUDE.md's tripwire table, and are gated by
# tools/PreProcessor/tests/test_instruction_budget.py — an untracked copy would
# mean every clone but one had no rules at all. Note the pattern has to exclude
# the directory's CONTENTS (`.claude/*`), not the directory: git does not descend
# into an excluded directory, so `!` cannot re-include a file underneath one —
# which is also why `rules/` is re-included as a DIRECTORY rather than as
# `!.claude/rules/*.md`. Per-machine overrides belong in `settings.local.json`,
# which stays ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/rules/

# Editor / tool backup copies. A `.bak` beside a tracked file is a local undo
# buffer, never an input — config/pipeline/*.hws.bak is how they turn up here.
*.bak

# Local working configs. The mesh parameter file and pipeline/workspace scripts
# are written per-experiment next to the case being tuned; the ones worth keeping
# live in config/pipeline/ under their own names and go in with `git add -f`.
#
# THAT LAST SENTENCE IS WHY THE GUI'S SAVE DIALOGS DEFAULT INTO `config/local/`
# AND NOT INTO `config/pipeline/`. A folder whose declared purpose is to hold
# force-added keepers can never be a safe save default: `config/pipeline/` carries
# README.md, template.json and three demo scripts that four tests read, so a
# session whose name collides with one is a single Enter away from overwriting a
# committed script in place — issue #5's defect with a different folder. It has
# already happened once: the blank session is named "Untitled 1", which is how
# `config/pipeline/Untitled 1.json` came to be tracked (c2a90c5), and
# `config/mesh/` holds two of the same accident.
#
# `config/local/` exists so the rule needs no per-file whack-a-mole: the whole
# directory is ignored, so it holds nothing tracked BY CONSTRUCTION, which is the
# property tests/test_save_dialog_defaults.py asks git about rather than reading
# from a hand-written list of folder names.
config/local/
#
# `config/mesh/` is ignored as a DIRECTORY rather than one file at a time: every
# file in it is a mesh parameter file the GUI wrote (`Background_para_<stem>.dat`),
# nothing curated has ever lived there, and the per-file line this replaces is
# what let two of them be committed by accident — the whack-a-mole this block was
# already losing. A reference grid parameter file worth keeping still goes in with
# `git add -f`, the same escape the curated pipeline scripts use.
config/mesh/
#
# Two named files under config/pipeline/, which cannot be ignored wholesale: it
# holds the curated scripts (README.md, template.json and three demos that four
# tests read). Both of these are the accident this policy exists to prevent — a
# GUI session's default name, accepted once and committed.
config/pipeline/cyl0d5_Rot1d0.hws
config/pipeline/Untitled 1.json
